{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-86-r1-instincts/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "1\timport type { Container } from \"@harbor/dispatch/types\";\n2\t\n3\tconst SEGREGATION: Record<string, readonly string[]> = {\n4\t  \"1\": [\"2.1\", \"3\", \"4.1\", \"5.1\", \"5.2\", \"8\"],\n5\t  \"2.1\": [\"1\", \"5.1\"],\n6\t  \"3\": [\"1\", \"5.1\", \"5.2\"],\n7\t  \"4.1\": [\"1\", \"5.1\"],\n8\t  \"5.1\": [\"1\", \"2.1\", \"3\", \"4.1\"],\n9\t  \"5.2\": [\"1\", \"3\"],\n10\t  \"8\": [\"1\"],\n11\t};\n12\t\n13\texport function primaryClass(dgClass: string): string {\n14\t  return dgClass.trim().split(\".\")[0];\n15\t}\n16\t\n17\texport function mustSegregate(a: string, b: string): boolean {\n18\t  const left = SEGREGATION[primaryClass(a)] ?? [];\n19\t  const right = SEGREGATION[primaryClass(b)] ?? [];\n20\t  return left.includes(primaryClass(b)) || right.includes(primaryClass(a));\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\texport function adjacentConflicts(row: readonly Container[]): Array<[string, string]> {\n24\t  const out: Array<[string, string]> = [];\n25\t  for (let i = 1; i < row.length; i++) {\n26\t    const a = row[i - 1];\n27\t    const b = row[i];\n28\t    if (a.dgClass && b.dgClass && mustSegregate(a.dgClass, b.dgClass)) {\n29\t      out.push([a.id, b.id]);\n30\t    }\n31\t  }\n32\t  return out;\n33\t}\n34\t", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01131wwipwX6wJicPe1rEmfT", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "9cd90b78-28ee-4764-95bf-68c08ddddabc", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:38:43.553Z", "toolUseResult": {}, "type": "user"}
{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-86-r1-instincts/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "Now I understand the issue. The problem is in the `mustSegregate` function. It's using `primaryClass()` to look up in the SEGREGATION table, but the table itself uses the full class:division format (like \"5.1\", not just \"5\"). This means classes with divisions are never found in the lookup.\n\nLet me fix this:", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV98neEX6gMbJtn29mgQ", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "9cd90b78-28ee-4764-95bf-68c08ddddabc", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:38:55.905Z", "type": "assistant"}
