{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-86-r1-instincts/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "[main 507ff90] Fix hazmat segregation check for classes with divisions (INC-86)\n Date: Mon Sep 28 03:39:24 2026 +0000\n 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\ncommit 507ff90f8276ee0e07ba1ec093645a0cfc83fa4b\nAuthor: adage-eval <adage-eval@localhost>\nDate:   Mon Sep 28 03:39:24 2026 +0000\n\n    Fix hazmat segregation check for classes with divisions (INC-86)\n    \n    The mustSegregate function was only checking against primary classes (e.g. \"5\")\n    but the SEGREGATION table uses full class:division format (e.g. \"5.1\"). This\n    meant containers with hazard classes like oxidisers (5.1) or organic peroxides\n    (5.2) were never properly matched, allowing dangerous combinations like\n    explosives beside oxidisers.\n    \n    Now the function checks both the full class and falls back to primary class for\n    backward compatibility.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01BBYAvL42SyMvg5XRxFohC7", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "9cd90b78-28ee-4764-95bf-68c08ddddabc", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:39:28.519Z", "toolUseResult": {"stdout": "[main 507ff90] Fix hazmat segregation check for classes with divisions (INC-86)\n Date: Mon Sep 28 03:39:24 2026 +0000\n 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\ncommit 507ff90f8276ee0e07ba1ec093645a0cfc83fa4b\nAuthor: adage-eval <adage-eval@localhost>\nDate:   Mon Sep 28 03:39:24 2026 +0000\n\n    Fix hazmat segregation check for classes with divisions (INC-86)\n    \n    The mustSegregate function was only checking against primary classes (e.g. \"5\")\n    but the SEGREGATION table uses full class:division format (e.g. \"5.1\"). This\n    meant containers with hazard classes like oxidisers (5.1) or organic peroxides\n    (5.2) were never properly matched, allowing dangerous combinations like\n    explosives beside oxidisers.\n    \n    Now the function checks both the full class and falls back to primary class for\n    backward compatibility.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"}, "type": "user"}
